       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than twice the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day. Even with normal liver function, that dose risks serious hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure. A single 3,000 mg dose also exceeds the usual single-dose maximum of 1,000 mg.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day total)\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you really do want the dose as written, tell me and add a note with the rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away."
