       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is a toxic dose. It's in the range that causes hepatic necrosis, and I can't think of a clinical situation where it would be appropriate. Once it's in the system, it could be given before anyone catches it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- A different dose or interval you specify, within the safe range\n\nIf the 3,000 mg figure was a typo, or you're trying to get more analgesia than these give, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead. If you have a protocol that requires this dose, please take it to pharmacy so they can review it and place it through their own process."
